From: Vyron Code D-11 local hardening (VYRON_CODE_D11_FINAL_EPHEMERAL_DIAGNOSTICS_PATCH)
Applies to: NousResearch/hermes-agent, installed local copy, version 0.21.0.

OPTIONAL, NOT APPLIED BY THIS TOOLING. Every attempt to write to Hermes's installed source from
inside this development environment has been refused by that environment's own permission
system, across two prior rounds and four distinct techniques (direct Edit, `git apply`, a Python
read/analysis script, and - this round - a fresh `git apply` attempt). This file exists so you
can review, and apply yourself, the exact change that closes the second persistence gap found in
this round: patch 0001 (`agent._persist_disabled = True`) correctly stops the SQLite session/
message store from writing anything durable, live-proven with two separate unique markers, but a
second, independent Hermes mechanism - an API-error debug dumper, and a per-turn info log line -
is not gated by that flag at all, and was live-proven (same markers) to still write prompt text
to disk.

WHAT IT DOES (four small hunks, three files):

  1. `agent/agent_runtime_helpers.py::dump_api_request_debug` - the single function behind every
     call to `agent._dump_api_request_debug(...)` (used for the opt-in `HERMES_DUMP_REQUESTS`
     preflight dump, and unconditionally for the non-retryable-client-error and
     max-retries-exhausted error paths). Adds one early return: if the calling agent has
     `_persist_disabled = True`, the function does nothing and no
     `sessions/request_dump_*.json` file is ever created. This is the single choke point for all
     three call sites, so one guard covers the opt-in preflight dump and both error paths.

  2. `agent/turn_context.py` - the per-turn `logger.info("conversation turn: ... msg=%r", ...)`
     line that runs on every turn (success or failure) and, until now, always included an 80-char
     preview of the user's actual message text. When `_persist_disabled` is set, the preview is
     replaced with a fixed placeholder; the rest of the line (session/model/provider/platform/
     history length) is unchanged, so operational log lines for ordinary, non-ephemeral agents
     are completely unaffected.

  3 & 4. `agent/turn_recovery.py` - two log lines that fire specifically on the non-retryable
     API-error path and can carry the raw provider error/response text (which, for some provider
     failure modes, can itself echo back request content): the `logger.error("... Non-retryable
     client error: %s", ...)` line, and the `logger.warning("API call failed ... summary=%s",
     ...)` line. Both redact only the error/summary text when `_persist_disabled` is set; retry
     count, error type, and provider/model context are unchanged, so error-rate monitoring for
     ordinary agents keeps working exactly as before.

WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT TOUCH:

  - The `[session_id]` tag every Hermes log line carries (via the logging session-context filter
    set up in `set_session_context()`), used by `hermes logs` to group lines per run. It is
    generic logging infrastructure that applies to every platform and every agent, not something
    tied to `dump_api_request_debug` or a specific log line's content, and it is an opaque
    correlator, not task content - de-scoping it keeps this patch to the narrowest change that
    actually stops task/response/error *content* from landing on disk, per the mission's own
    instruction not to globally disable diagnostics.
  - Any non-`api_server` platform, or any `api_server` agent that does NOT have
    `_persist_disabled = True` set (i.e. every guard is conditional on that exact flag, which
    only patch 0001 sets, and only for API Server task agents).

HOW TO APPLY (PowerShell, run as the same user who owns the Hermes installation):
  1. Back up first:
       $ts = Get-Date -Format "yyyyMMdd_HHmmss"
       Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\agent_runtime_helpers.py" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\agent_runtime_helpers.py.vyron-pre-diag-patch-$ts.bak"
       Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_context.py" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_context.py.vyron-pre-diag-patch-$ts.bak"
       Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_recovery.py" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_recovery.py.vyron-pre-diag-patch-$ts.bak"
  2. From this repository root:
       git apply --directory="$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent" hermes-patches/0002-api-server-ephemeral-diagnostics.patch
     (or apply the hunks below by hand if `git apply` complains about line-ending/context
     differences against your installed copy's exact version.)
  3. Restart Hermes: stop any running `hermes gateway run`, then start it again.

HOW TO ROLL BACK:
  Restore the three `.bak` files created in step 1 over their originals, then restart Hermes.

